{"Resource Owner Mismatch: Per-client and all-clients resources are created with owner resourceServer.getClientId(), but the new evaluator looks them up with server.getId(). When those identifiers differ, V2 checks miss the resource that stores the client permission and either deny a granted client-specific permission or evaluate against the wrong fallback resource.": 0.7830296754837036, "Typed Lookup Misses Clients: The listing only scans resources whose stored type is Clients, but per-client resources created for object permissions are not assigned that type. A user granted access to a specific client can pass the direct permission check while filtered client listing still returns no matching client.": 0.6031443476676941, "V2 Removal Cleanup Throws: When V2 admin permissions are active, management(...) returns MgmtPermissionsV2, so this client-removal listener calls ClientPermissionsV2.setPermissionsEnabled(...). That method throws UnsupportedOperationException, which can turn client deletion into a server error instead of completing the cleanup path.": 0.8625974059104919}